      "value": "@{62df7cd83e007e467295c4e1|full_name} As far as I know, the easiest way to have an idea of how optimized a world is either by looking at the MB size or if the Title or Description says it directly. I honestly don't know how it would be determined, I'm not that knowledgeable when it comes to world and avatar creation, though I might start getting into it at some point.\n\nAll I'm saying with this post is that it would be beneficial for players (especially those on Standalone Quest) to have an indicator or some kind of performance reading that will give them a heads up of what they might be getting into. I remember countless times from being on just quest and loading into a world that has no indication of it being unoptimized yet being open to quest, and then either causing terrible lag or straight up crashing.\n\nHow this post isn't getting any attention (even a little) other than yours  is crazy to me.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
